==English==
{{was wotd|2025|January|13}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|bumper|t1=(''noun'') thing which is particularly abundant, excellent, or large; (''adjective'') particularly abundant, excellent, or large|crop|notext=1|type=endocentric}}, originally referring to a very large harvest of a crop.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbʌmpə ˌkɹɒp/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbʌmpəɹ ˌkɹɑp/|a=GA}}
* {{hyphenation|en|bump|er crop}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} An [[excess#Noun|excess]] of something; a [[large#Adjective|large]] [[yield#Noun|yield]].
#: {{ux|en|The kindergarten seems to have a '''bumper crop''' of new children this year.}}

